cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite this software release (and the article, once published)."
title: "NPM1-mutated AML: FLT3-ITD vs FLT3-TKD by DNMT3A/TET2 status - multi-cohort public-data analysis (code and results)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible code, pre-specified protocol, data provenance and reference results for a multi-cohort
  public-data analysis (TCGA-LAML and Beat AML via cBioPortal; AMLSG) testing whether DNMT3A/TET2
  co-mutation modifies the overall-survival difference between FLT3-ITD and FLT3-TKD in adults with
  NPM1-mutated acute myeloid leukemia. A single command downloads the public source data, harmonises
  variants, runs cohort-stratified Cox models with sensitivity analyses and a 2,000-replicate bootstrap,
  regenerates all tables and figures, and checks the re-run against the reported estimates.
